Generate 0035-game-3d-camera-export.patch.

SF64 game-side exports for stereoscopic 3D (0034 consumes them). SF64 has no
z_view/Camera class — it composes the gameplay view with a global
Matrix_LookAt(gPlayCamEye, gPlayCamAt, playerCamUp) in fox_display.c.

- Edit 1 (fox_display.c, after the LookAt): export the camera basis
  (eye/fwd/right, P00, dist) so 0034 folds the eye offset in the CAMERA basis
  (the combined view*projection can't be decomposed). Plus comfort flags:
  gSoh3DPaused (PLAY_PAUSE) and gSoh3DCinematic (cutscene/transition — level
  intro/complete, warp, 360, boss moments, ending) which eases stereo depth
  toward a hardcoded 15% while set. This block runs ONLY in GSTATE_PLAY
  (Display_Update is the DRAW_PLAY draw path).

- Edit 2 (fox_game.c, in Game_Update — device round 4): the AUTHORITATIVE
  per-frame stereo gate. Because edit 1 only runs during play, gSoh3DInPlay
  would stay STALE at 1 on the map / menu / game-over / results screens after
  a level, leaving those "world progress" screens rendering in 3D
  (disorienting — user report). Game_Update runs for EVERY game state, so
  setting gSoh3DInPlay = (gGameState == GSTATE_PLAY) here forces those screens
  flat (0034 fades separation to 0 when !InPlay). Also exports gGameState for
  the `3d` bridge telemetry.

Device round 4 removed the per-object Arwing depth sentinels (0x5C/0x5D
around the player draws): the fold demonstrably reached the ship
(objFold telemetry) but the reduction was not perceivable on-device, so per
the user we stopped targeting the ship and let the single overall Depth
slider compensate. The 0034 objSepMul machinery is now inert (no sentinels
emit) and harmless.

fox_display.c / fox_game.c are C (no extern "C"); sqrtf/tanf already used
in-file. __IOS__-guarded so the macOS build compiles this vendor and links
no shell.

--- a/src/engine/fox_display.c
+++ b/src/engine/fox_display.c
@@ -1946,6 +1946,57 @@
     Matrix_Push(&gGfxMatrix);
     Matrix_LookAt(gGfxMatrix, gPlayCamEye.x, gPlayCamEye.y, gPlayCamEye.z, gPlayCamAt.x, gPlayCamAt.y, gPlayCamAt.z,
                   playerCamUp.x, playerCamUp.y, playerCamUp.z, MTXF_APPLY);
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0035): export the camera basis for stereoscopic 3D (0034)
+    // at the exact values Matrix_LookAt consumed.
+    {
+        extern volatile float gSoh3DCamDist, gSoh3DCamP00;
+        extern volatile float gSoh3DCamRight[3], gSoh3DCamFwd[3], gSoh3DCamEye[3];
+        extern volatile int gSoh3DPaused, gSoh3DInPlay, gSoh3DCinematic;
+        extern f32 gFovY;
+        f32 sohFx = gPlayCamAt.x - gPlayCamEye.x;
+        f32 sohFy = gPlayCamAt.y - gPlayCamEye.y;
+        f32 sohFz = gPlayCamAt.z - gPlayCamEye.z;
+        f32 sohDist = sqrtf(sohFx * sohFx + sohFy * sohFy + sohFz * sohFz);
+        if (sohDist > 0.0f) {
+            sohFx /= sohDist;
+            sohFy /= sohDist;
+            sohFz /= sohDist;
+            f32 sohRx = sohFy * playerCamUp.z - sohFz * playerCamUp.y;
+            f32 sohRy = sohFz * playerCamUp.x - sohFx * playerCamUp.z;
+            f32 sohRz = sohFx * playerCamUp.y - sohFy * playerCamUp.x;
+            f32 sohRl = sqrtf(sohRx * sohRx + sohRy * sohRy + sohRz * sohRz);
+            if (sohRl > 1e-4f) {
+                gSoh3DCamRight[0] = sohRx / sohRl;
+                gSoh3DCamRight[1] = sohRy / sohRl;
+                gSoh3DCamRight[2] = sohRz / sohRl;
+                gSoh3DCamFwd[0] = sohFx;
+                gSoh3DCamFwd[1] = sohFy;
+                gSoh3DCamFwd[2] = sohFz;
+                gSoh3DCamEye[0] = gPlayCamEye.x;
+                gSoh3DCamEye[1] = gPlayCamEye.y;
+                gSoh3DCamEye[2] = gPlayCamEye.z;
+                f32 sohHalfFovX =
+                    tanf(gFovY * 0.5f * (3.14159265f / 180.0f)) * ((f32) SCREEN_WIDTH / (f32) SCREEN_HEIGHT);
+                gSoh3DCamP00 = (sohHalfFovX > 1e-4f) ? (1.0f / sohHalfFovX) : 1.0f;
+                gSoh3DCamDist = sohDist;
+            }
+        }
+        gSoh3DPaused = (gPlayState == PLAY_PAUSE);
+        gSoh3DInPlay = (gGameState == GSTATE_PLAY);
+        // Cutscene/transition detection. SF64 has no cutscene game-state, but
+        // cinematic moments live in gPlayer[0].state (plus the ending). 0034
+        // eases stereo depth toward a hardcoded 15% while set. U_TURN (a
+        // gameplay somersault) is deliberately excluded.
+        gSoh3DCinematic = (gGameState == GSTATE_ENDING) ||
+                          (gPlayer[0].state == PLAYERSTATE_LEVEL_INTRO) ||
+                          (gPlayer[0].state == PLAYERSTATE_LEVEL_COMPLETE) ||
+                          (gPlayer[0].state == PLAYERSTATE_ENTER_WARP_ZONE) ||
+                          (gPlayer[0].state == PLAYERSTATE_START_360) ||
+                          (gPlayer[0].state == PLAYERSTATE_GFOX_REPAIR) ||
+                          (gPlayer[0].state == PLAYERSTATE_ANDROSS_MOUTH);
+    }
+#endif
 
